--TEST--
A reflective call to a `private` method fails from outside the class and runs from inside it, each the way the ordinary call at that site does — `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`: acting on a member runs
// through exactly the check ordinary code *at that call site* would face. So
// this asks the question as an **agreement** rather than as a refusal: the
// same method, reached through both doors from each of two sites, with the
// answers compared. A `call` that simply refused every `private` method would
// print plausibly on the first half alone and fail on the second.
class Vault {
    public function open(): string {
        return "opened";
    }

    private function sealed(): string {
        return "the combination";
    }

    // Inside the class, an ordinary call to `sealed()` compiles, so the
    // reflective one written here reaches it too — and answers the same thing.
    public function fromInside(): tainted string {
        var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject($this);
        var $reflective = $described->call($this, "sealed", []);
        if ($reflective == $this->sealed()) {
            return "inside agrees: " . $reflective;
        }
        return "inside disagrees";
    }
}

var $vault = new Vault();
var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject($vault);

// The public half runs through both doors, so the agreement below is not two
// doors that are simply both shut.
mixed $erased = $vault;
echo $described->call($vault, "open", []), " ", $erased->open(), "\n";

// The ordinary call to a `private` method from out here is the one through an
// erased receiver: a `mixed` is outside every class by construction, which is
// the premise this call site has too. Both refusals are caught as `LogicError`
// and compared by their own sentence — the same check, not two that agree.
var $reflectively = "not refused";
try {
    var $said = $described->call($vault, "sealed", []);
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    $reflectively = $refused->message;
}
var $ordinarily = "not refused";
try {
    var $also = $erased->sealed();
} catch (LogicError $met) {
    $ordinarily = $met->message;
}
if ($reflectively == $ordinarily) {
    echo "outside agrees: ", $reflectively, "\n";
} else {
    echo "outside disagrees: ", $reflectively, " / ", $ordinarily, "\n";
}

// And from inside the class, where the ordinary call is allowed.
echo $vault->fromInside(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
opened opened
outside agrees: `Vault::sealed` is not public, and a `mixed` receiver is outside every class
inside agrees: the combination
